ackground:whitesmoke\"><a name=\"m_-634918917012478050_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/israel-r-user-group/t/7a8f17d5e2050dc9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/israel-r-user-group/t/7a8f17d5e2050dc9&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498578551000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vgBegvqFmNo7x6MqIXmDI\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\">question about igraph package</span></a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\"><b>amit gal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">amit...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</b> Aug 24 05:26PM +0300  <br><br>Hi,<br> <br>I&#39;m trying to work with some network structures in R and use igraph<br>package. I&#39;m mainly interested in dynamic aspects of my networks, so I<br>start with an initial network and then do a lot of add.vertices and<br>add.edges operations.<br>now, here is my problem:<br>in one of my networks my edges are in fact weighted edges. when I &quot;add&quot; an<br>edge I want that if there is no existing edge between the given nodes, then<br>a new edge with the given weight will be added. However, if there is<br>already an edge between the given nodes, I don&#39;t want a new (parallel) edge<br>to be created, but rather, I want that the new weight will be added to the<br>existing weight.<br> <br>I don&#39;t know how to do that.<br>any suggestions?<br> <br>thanks,<br> <br>amit<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></p><div><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"color:#555555\">You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Group israel-r-user-group.<br>You can <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\">post via email</span></a>.<br>To unsubscribe from this group, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><spa